  "description": "T-4699: pivot blank rows and collapsed items beyond an outer row field. Data!A1:D9 has Region, Product, Size and Val over eight records: East A S 10, East A L 4, East B S 5, East B L 2, West A S 7, West B S 3, West B L 1, West C L 6 (numbers only). Each sheet is one builder-v2 pivot at A3, data Sum of Val unless noted; compact form unless noted, tabular means outline 0 and compact 0 on the table and every field. BI and BI2: rows Region, Product with insertBlankRow on the innermost Product, compact and tabular. BC: rows Region, columns Product, Size with insertBlankRow on the column field Product. BS and BS2: rows Region, Product with insertBlankRow on Region and East collapsed (item sd=0), compact and tabular. CC: rows Region, columns Product, Size with Product A collapsed. CB: East collapsed on a Region with subtotalTop 0. CU and CU2: East collapsed on a Region with custom subtotals count and max, compact and tabular. CR: Region with all eleven custom subtotals listed in reverse (varP, var, stdDevP, stdDev, count, product, min, max, avg, countA, sum), compact. CM and CM2: rows Region, Product, Size with Product A collapsed (a middle field), compact and tabular. CV: rows Region, Values with Sum of Val and Count of Val and East collapsed; CV2 the same with Product inside Values; CV3 rows Region, Product, Values (Values inside the field inside the collapsed item); CV4 is CV3 in tabular form. OC: plain outline form (compact 0 on the table and fields, outline on), Region with custom subtotals sum and count. Pivot cells are in the sidecar's `pivots` section; Q!A1 makes the case scored.",
